<StarlightPage
	frontmatter={{
		title: 'Claude Certification (CCA-F), Explained',
		description:
			'What Anthropic\'s Claude Certified Architect credential is, who can take it today, and where the official details, including registration, live.',
		template: 'splash',
		tableOfContents: false,
	}}
>
	<p class="cert-verified">Facts on this page were verified against Anthropic's public pages as of {VERIFIED_AS_OF}. Certification programs change; always confirm on Anthropic's official pages.</p>

	<p>
		In March 2026, Anthropic launched its first technical certification: the
		<strong>Claude Certified Architect, Foundations (CCA-F)</strong>. If you have seen the
		name on LinkedIn and wondered what it actually is, whether you can take it, and where
		the real information lives, this page collects the publicly verifiable facts in one place.
	</p>

	<h2>What it is</h2>
	<p>
		Anthropic announced the certification on March 12, 2026 as part of its
		<a href="https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-partner-network">Claude Partner Network</a> launch,
		describing it as "a technical exam for solution architects building production applications
		with Claude." The certification's own page says it "validates that practitioners can make
		informed decisions about tradeoffs when implementing real-world solutions with Claude,"
		across four core technologies: Claude Code, the Claude Agent SDK, the Claude API, and
		Model Context Protocol (MCP).
	</p>
	<p>
		The exam guide on Anthropic's Partner Academy page describes the exam's format and
		content domains. That guide, together with the certification terms and the exam policy,
		is linked from the official exam page, and it is the document to read first.
	</p>

	<h2>Who can take the CCA-F today?</h2>
	<p>
		As of {VERIFIED_AS_OF}, the certification is offered through Anthropic's partner program:
		it launched as available "today for partners," and Anthropic's July 2026 article on its
		role-based certifications says "Exams are available to members of the Claude Partner
		Network." Exams are delivered by Pearson VUE, and the credential is earned by an
		individual person. It is not generally available to the public. Anthropic now lists four
		Claude certifications in total, with Claude Certified Architect, Foundations as the one
		that launched first.
	</p>
	<p>
		If that is disappointing, here is the useful reframe: the skills the certification names
		are all publicly teachable today. Claude Academy offers free courses from Anthropic's
		education team on Claude and AI, open to everyone, though completing them is not the
		same as earning the certification.
	</p>

	<h2>Fees and registration</h2>
	<p>
		Anthropic's public pages do not list the exam fee. Registration runs through
		<a href="https://anthropic-partners.skilljar.com/claude-certified-architect-foundations-certification">Anthropic Partner Academy</a>,
		and scheduling is through Pearson VUE. Check those pages for current details before registering.
	</p>
	<p>
		Pearson VUE lists this exam as Claude Certified Architect: Foundations (CCAR-F), so you may
		see that code there. This page uses the shorthand CCA-F.
	</p>

	<h2>Where the official details live</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-partner-network">The Claude Partner Network announcement</a>, where the certification debuted.</li>
		<li><a href="https://claude.com/resources/articles/four-role-based-claude-certifications">Anthropic's article on its four role-based certifications</a>, which states who can take the exams.</li>
		<li><a href="https://www.pearsonvue.com/us/en/anthropic.html">The Pearson VUE page for the Claude certification program</a>, where exams are delivered.</li>
		<li><a href="https://anthropic-partners.skilljar.com/claude-certified-architect-foundations-certification">The official certification page</a> on Anthropic Partner Academy, with the exam guide, terms, and policy documents.</li>
		<li><a href="https://academy.claude.com/">Claude Academy</a>, the free public course catalog.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Building the skills in the meantime</h2>
	<p>
		Clawdemy's free
		<a href="/tracks/engineering-agentic-systems/">Engineering Agentic Systems</a>
		track teaches the underlying skills, from agentic architecture and tool design to
		orchestration and reliability, with no signup and no fee.
	</p>

